  "description": "*“If you let me make rice cake, I won’t eat you.”*\n\nWhile crossing the mountain in the middle of the night to find medicinal herbs for his sick mother, the filial son Park Dal-Jae encounters a fearsome thousand-year-old tiger and the mountain master, Baek-Ho. When he suddenly gave rice cake to the tiger who was looking for rice cake, wow! What it bit was not my neck or the rice cake I held out, but a large pepper(?) hanging between its legs.\n\n *“Oh, oh. The pepper is gone!”\n“Stop. I’ll suck it out and return it to its original state.”*\n\nWhere did something so delicious come from!\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)\n\n*Note: Includes three extra chapters.*",
